{
    "background_story": "Joseph was a brilliant physicist who had spent his entire career studying the mysteries of time and space. His life's work was focused on achieving the impossible: creating a state of stasis, where time would appear to stand still. After years of tireless research and experimentation, Joseph finally succeeded in building a functioning stasis chamber. He became the first human test subject, stepping into the chamber and activating the device. As the machine hummed to life, Joseph felt his body slow to a near-stop, his aging process halted. For what felt like an eternity, he remained frozen in time, observing the world around him through a haze of suspended animation. When the chamber was finally opened, Joseph emerged, unchanged, while the world outside had moved on decades. His achievement had granted him a unique perspective on the nature of time itself.",
